notes               = "Untitled in source. Same date as page 144. IMPORTANT — the ===lantern=== on this poem is BEN'S OWN pencil rendering from the margin of the printed page, dated '5 June 2022', not an agent's: it is reproduced verbatim including his spelling of 'hurridly'. This follows the page-70 / stay-go precedent that lantern can hold a human draft. His reading of گفت نشینم... برخیزم as 'she said - don't sit... I rose' differs from the literal pass, which takes the line as the dew's two deliberative questions ('shall I settle... shall I rise'); both readings are live and the difference is recorded in raw photos/persian_poems.md. 12 Ordibehesht = 2 May 1993. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
