===persian===

ابر شبنم شد....
بر دشت نشست....
آهویی تند گذشت....
زیر پایِ آهو شبنم له شد....
گفت نشینم... برخیزم...
یاد دریا افتاد...
عشق پیدا شد و...
شبنم... مِه...
۱۳۷۲/۲/۱۲

===machine===

The cloud became dew....
It settled on the plain....
A deer went past at speed....
Under the deer's foot the dew was crushed....
It said: shall I settle... shall I rise...
It remembered the sea...
Love came to light and...
dew... became mist...
1372/2/12

===lantern===

clouds became dew...
she sat on the prairie...
A deer passed hurridly...
crushed dew beneath hoof...
she said - don't sit... I rose...
she remembered the sea...
found love... and...
dew..... fog...

===translation===

===footnotes===

The whole life of the poem is four seconds long: a cloud settles as dew, a deer treads on
it, and the crushed drop remembers the sea it came from and goes back up as mist. The Persian
گفت نشینم... برخیزم can be the dew asking itself whether to stay or rise, or an instruction given
to it; the poem does not settle which.
